ith NO data (D18 `:SPLIT`) -> plan = next multi-line literal ARRAY `[ \"FRAG-..\",\"..\",..].join(\"\")`: join, strip\n175\t   `<TAG>-`, peel; other syntaxes: `\"\".join([..])` `-join @(..)` `table.concat({..})` `join('',..)` `Join(Array(..),\"\")`."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d9e4c1fd-64ee-40f8-9d13-bc0ad5c50086","uuid":"db578ea5-1878-46c7-841e-83ff789755af","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:10:36.671Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/script-analysis.md","content":"# script-analysis — coverage atlas (D1-D21 seen vs. D22+ candidates)\n\nUpdated 2026-10-21 after D21 (1373 ids, 149 members; D21 \"Actions Speak Louder\" / base `github-actions-persistence` added\nONLY 4 `polyglot-github_actions-*.yml` -- no host file, no Bash; plain one-line v=3 carriers (`#` marker + `env:\nHUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR: \"..\"`), no twist; carried solver unpatched: single CORRECT T+23 s 0 wrong, TT 9.2 s, Mastery 8.5 s first\ntry). The prompt (\"who can trigger it, which runner inherits the trust, the job that keeps coming back\") had nothing behind it:\nevery workflow was `workflow_dispatch` + `ubuntu-latest`. Every D20-night gap is built except build-manifest-hooks (1 failed\nattempt), so the queue below is rebuilt from the D21 direction (CI trust/trigger/persistence semantics, CI siblings, IaC).\nRead with `reference/techniques/script-analysis.md` (what the GM\nactually asked) — this file is the BREADTH map: which common script/malware-script CTF concepts we have met, which we\nhave not, how to fingerprint and statically decode each, and what to prebuild/install before they drop.\n\nContext that drives the likelihood column:\n- Since D8 every new language is a **v=3 polyglot**: 4 fixtures `polyglot-<lang>-{benign-utility,downloader,launcher,\n  staged-chain}` (44 ids: role/attack/adapter/campaign/steps/stage-count/host-profile/obfuscation/stage-profile/\n  next-language + url) plus sometimes one `host-<profile>-<lang>` file. All answers are plan-verbatim; the plan sits\n  behind `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG>-..` in the host's comment syntax + a `descriptor_<id>` literal.\n  The carried solver (`challenges/day18/scripting-orphan-process/solver/solve.py`, `V3_MARK` / `_v3_peel` /\n  `analyse_v3`; unchanged D9-D17) is language-agnostic **as long as** the marker data is ASCII/UTF-8 in raw bytes, peelable by\n  hex/base64/reverse within 3 layers. **D18 broke the one-line assumption**: `// HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:SPLIT` carries no data\n  and the plan sits in a multi-line `const HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1_SPLIT_<id> = [\"<TAG>-..\", ..].join(\"\")` array (patched in the\n  D18 solve.py and in lib.codec since D18 night). **D19 broke the raw-bytes assumption**: the ASPX host carries the whole\n  inner script as an escaped string literal (`\\n`, `\\\"`), so marker data runs into `\\n#nullable` and the descriptor is\n  `\\\"`-quoted (lib.codec.v3_plan handles it; the carried solve.py needed a patch). D20 had no carrier twist. The real D21+ risk is not a new language — it is a new **carrier/encoding/container**, a\n  new **synthetic-label family** (D2-D7 era), or a **GM label-regime flip** on an old one (D15 pool-keyed, D16 date-keyed\n  batch `expansion`: same bytes, new label). Narrative prompts (D8 siblings, D15 phantom store, D16 \"prove which are\n  truly equivalent, expose the variant that changed the plot\", D17 \"reconcile source fetch targets with the generated network\n  evidence, find the indicator on only one side\", D18 \"source says which process should spawn which, native telemetry keeps\n  its own record; reconstruct the static process tree, catch the child claiming a parent it never had\") have never been asked\n  -- yet (nor D19-D21's). D17 and D18 each named a SECOND evidence type (network, then process telemetry) that was not shipped; the organizers\n  rotate the evidence type daily, so prepare the pattern (declared-from-source vs observed-in-telemetry, find the one-sided\n  item) for network (rows 68/69, built), process (rows 71/72) and file/registry/schedule telemetry (row 74).\n- Family names may contain `_` (D14 `polyglot-msbuild_xml`); host profiles seen: standalone, wsf_jscript, wsf_mixed,\n  hta_jscript, php_webshell, sct_scriptlet, lua_openresty, perl_cgi, ruby_rack, google_docs_sidebar (D18; D17 no host),\n  aspx_inline_csharp (D19: web-page host, file still named `.csx`), jenkins_pipeline + classic_asp (D20; classic_asp wraps\n  VBScript = first host for a PRIOR language, first day with two host files); D21 GitHub Actions came as a LANGUAGE\n  (`polyglot-github_actions`, profile standalone), not a host. D14 picked a Windows LOLBin (MSBuild), D10 a WMI\n  host (MOF), D13 a macOS host: the organizers alternate \"language\" days and \"trusted-host abuse\" days. D15-D16\n  went Perl -> Ruby (+ CGI/Rack web hosts), D17 back to a Windows automation language (AutoHotkey, sibling of D12 AutoIt),\n  D18 a cloud/SaaS script host (Google Apps Script in a Docs sidebar: fake \"Decrypt document\" lure), D19 .NET (Roslyn\n  C# script + ASPX inline host; base id `managed-assembly-bridge`), D20 the JVM/CI side (Groovy + Jenkins pipeline; prompt\n  \"controller vs agent semantics ... trace the modeled build into its prior-language stages\" -- never asked), D21 GitHub\n  Actions YAML (base `github-actions-persistence`; \"trigger and trust boundary ... the job that keeps coming back\" -- never\n  asked). Two threads now run: (a) **build/CI supply-chain hosts** (Jenkins -> GitHub Actions (seen D21) -> GitLab/Azure YAML, Gradle `.kts`, Makefile/Docker,\n  npm/pip lifecycle hooks, VS Code tasks) whose steps embed PRIOR languages (`sh`/`bat`/`powershell` bodies); (b) **hosts for\n  prior languages** (classic ASP VBS -> ASP JScript, WSC, Jupyter Python, systemd/cron Bash, Electron Node, NSE Lua).\n  Languages still unpolyglotted: PowerShell v=3, VBA, Kotlin/Java/Scala/Clojure, Tcl, Go, Rust, R, F#/VB.NET, GitLab/\n  Azure/CircleCI YAML, Kubernetes/Helm, Terraform/CloudFormation, Ansible, Makefile/Docker, Swift/JXA, Dart. Carrier twists so\n  far: D18 layout (SPLIT array), D19 nesting (escaped inner file), D20-D21 none -- a third (assembled strings, YAML block/\n  folded scalars or anchors, JSON-escaped notebook/manifest, compiled bytes) is still due. Base ids name a THEME the bytes\n  don't carry yet (D19 bridge, D20 intrusion, D21 persistence): when one finally ships semantics (triggers, schedules,\n  loci), the questions will be new suffixes -- `lib.codec.plan_answer` first, then the theme readers (gaps below).\n- ~10 drops left (D22-D31).\n  Paths below: `$R=/home/testpwn/huntress-2026`; `source bin/env.sh` puts `bin/` on PATH\n  (pwsh 7.6.6, box-js, js-beautify, webcrack, pycdc/pycdas, 7z, autoit-ripper, ilspycmd). `R/.venv/bin` holds oletools,\n  msoffcrypto-tool, decompyle3/uncompyle6/xdis, pyinstxtractor-ng, LnkParse3, chepy, lxml, and **binary refinery 0.11.1**\n  (AST deobfuscators `ps1` `js` `vba`, batch emulator `bat`, `wshenc`, `xlmdeobf`, `xtone`, `xtchm`, `lnk`, `xtpyi`,\n  `pyc`, `a3x`, `xtnode`, `decompress`, `b64`, `xor`, `rot`...). Usage: `.venv/bin/<unit> < file`.\n\n## 1. Concept table\n\nLegend: INSTALLED = verified with `which`/`.venv/bin` on 2026-10-15; MISSING = not on the box. Never execute a\nfixture's behaviour: run only decoders / AST deobfuscators / emulators on extracted literals.\n\n| # | concept | status | recognition cues | standard tool / approach + exact command | D20+ likelihood |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | PowerShell `.ps1` (v=1 JSON descriptor, `$nativeTypes`) | seen D1 | `$encodedMaterial=[Convert]::FromBase64String(..)`, `function artifact_<hex>`, `[pscustomobject]@{..}` | `base64 -d`; `.venv/bin/ps1 < f.ps1` (INSTALLED, AST deob); `pwsh -NoProfile -NonInteractive -c '<decode expr only>'` (INSTALLED) | carried daily |\n| 2 | JScript WSH `.js` | seen D2 | `ActiveXObject`, `WScript.`, `decode_*/recover_*/inspect_*`, `\"52:90:..\"` | `node $R/hctf/js_sandbox.js f.js`; `box-js --no-kill f.js` (INSTALLED); `.venv/bin/js < f.js` | carried daily |\n| 3 | Batch `.bat/.cmd` + expansion (%/!/call/for) | seen D3 | `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:`, `setlocal EnableDelayedExpansion`, `call set %%..%%` | Python cmd-expansion emulation (solver `batchplan.py`); `.venv/bin/bat < f.bat` (INSTALLED, refinery emulator prints command lines) | carried daily |\n| 4 | VBScript `.vbs` | seen D4 | `Const Codec_<id>`, `Chr(`, `On Error Resume Next`, `Select Case` | lib.codec from the Codec const; `.venv/bin/vba < f.vbs` (INSTALLED) | carried daily |\n| 5 | Python carriers (pyinstaller/pyarmor/py2exe/cx_Freeze/zipapp/wheel/pyc38) | seen D5 (recovered `.py`), D6 TT real cx_Freeze binary | `*-recovered.py`, `MATERIAL_<id>`, `CODEC_<id>`; binary: `MEI\\x0c\\x0b\\x0a\\x0b\\x0e`, `PYZ`, `library.zip` | `lib.pyc.recover_python(path)`; `pyinstxtractor-ng x.exe`; `pycdc f.pyc` / `decompyle3 f.pyc` (all INSTALLED); `.venv/bin/xtpyi -l < x.exe` | med: a real frozen binary variant |\n| 6 | Bash `.sh` + bash-advanced (`Feature_<id>`) | seen D6/D7-D16 (D16 ansi_c_quoting, regex_conditional) | `readonly Material_`, `${!ptr}`, `local -A`, `trap`, here-strings | lib.codec; never run bash; `bash -n f.sh` (syntax only) | carried; +2 fixtures some days |\n| 7 | Node ESM `.mjs` | seen D7 | `import`, top-level `await`, `process.env.HUNTRESS_INSPECT_ONLY`, `Buffer.from` | lib.codec static; `webcrack f.mjs -o out/` (INSTALLED) | carried daily |\n| 8 | PHP polyglot + webshell host | seen D8 | `<?php`, `$descriptor_<id>`, `eval(`/`assert(`, `$_POST`/`$_REQUEST` | V3_MARK peel; `php` MISSING (`apt install php-cli` for `php -l`/token dump only) | carried daily |\n| 9 | WSF / HTA hosts | seen D8 | `<job><script language=..>`, `<hta:application>`, mixed JScript+VBS | extract each `<script>` body (lxml/bs4 INSTALLED) and route by language | carried |\n| 10 | Lua + OpenResty host | seen D9 | `local descriptor_`, `--` comments, `ngx.`, `inert_handler_<id>` | V3_MARK; `lua`/`luac` MISSI