{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018xoUhfoYnEmAP4Pix7V4LS","type":"tool_result","content":"176\t marker data running into `\\n..` / descriptor `= \\\"..\\\"` (D19 ASPX: inner script is an ESCAPED string) -> unescape `\\n \\\" \\\\`\n177\t   (`\"\"`, `&quot;`, CDATA, `\\u0022`) and rescan. A v=3 file with no plan = CARRIER bug: call lib.codec.v3_plan(text) first\n178\t   (it read D18 + D19), then fix the read -- never walk role/attack enums or put a guessed value in a bulk POST.\n179\t descriptor syntaxes to accept: `x = \"..\"` `x := \"..\"` `set x \"..\"`/`set x {..}` `x <- \"..\"` `X: &str = \"..\"`\n180\t   `DESCRIPTOR_X = \"..\"` (Ruby const, seen D16) `descriptor_x: \"..\"` (YAML) `<HuntressDescriptor>..</..>` (XML) heredoc/block scalar\n181\t material may wrap (`|` YAML, `=begin`, `<# #>`, `\"\"\"`, `\\`, `.`/`+`/`&`/`..` concat): join pieces, strip separators, THEN peel\n182\t peel by SHAPE, max 4 layers, accept only output starting `v=` (or `{` JSON): hex (any separators) | base64 std/urlsafe\n183\t   (also reversed text) | base32 [A-Z2-7=] | base85/ascii85 <~~> | gzip H4sI / zlib eJ eN eF | rot13 | %xx | \\xNN \\NNN \\ddd\n184\t   \\uXXXX \\u{..} | int lists (READ the radix from code) | UTF-16LE inside b64 (PS -enc: every 2nd byte 00)\n185\t copy plan values verbatim (role, attack, adapter, steps, profiles, next_language); never derive them from code\n186\tLAYERED OBFUSCATION -> standard tool (static, no network, no exec of behaviour):\n187\t PowerShell   .venv/bin/ps1 < f  (folds -f reorder, `ticks, 'a'+'b', [char]N, -join, -replace, .Invoke)\n188\t JS           webcrack f.js -o out/  (obfuscator.io arrays) | .venv/bin/js < f | node hctf/js_sandbox.js f (eval->capture)\n189\t VBA/VBS      .venv/bin/olevba --decode --deobf f | .venv/bin/vba < f.bas | pcodedmp f.doc (stomped p-code)\n190\t Batch        .venv/bin/bat < f  (emulates set/%x:~a,b%/%x:a=b%/^/delayed !x!; prints commands, runs nothing)\n191\t XLM .venv/bin/xlmdeobf | OneNote xtone -l | CHM xtchm -l | LNK .venv/bin/lnk | AutoIt autoit-ripper x.exe out/, a3x\n192\t Python       swap exec/eval->print, run with python3 -I in an empty dir; marshal blob -> pycdc / xdis (match version)\n193\t compressed   .venv/bin/b64 < blob | .venv/bin/decompress   (gzip/zlib/raw deflate/lzma/bz2 auto)\n194\t PHP chains   apply the named functions innermost-first in Python (base64_decode, gzinflate=raw deflate, str_rot13, strrev)\n195\tNEVER: run the fixture's interpreter on the file (ruby/perl/php/tclsh/Rscript/make/go run/msbuild/pwsh -File);\n196\t `perl -MO=Deparse` and `make -n` still execute BEGIN/$(shell) -> strip first; apply XSLT; open URLs from the plan.\n197\tSYNTHETIC LABELS (if a new language brings code-shape questions): read accepted_values; compose `<keyword>_guard`,\n198\t `<keyword>_once`, `<keyword>_<action>`. Batch `expansion` = STATEMENT-ONLY table by default (D15+); a carried label rejected\n199\t on unchanged bytes = GM regime moved: tabulate (construct, label) vs started_at/run_for_time/variant_fresh first.\n200\tEQUIVALENCE/OUTLIER prompt (D16): only if asked; compare lib.codec.plan_canonical (role/steps/adapter/attack/profiles).\n201\tNETWORK-RECONCILE prompt (D17 \"source vs network evidence, indicator on one side\"): flavour unless a question/net file exists;\n202\t then lib.codec.network_indicators(bytes) (pcap/HAR/Zeek/Sysmon 3,22) + reconcile({member: plan}, bytes) -> reconcile_answer\n203\t (r, kind, accepted, what=). Graph ids: download_graph(plans) -> download_graph_answer. Unknown plan-key suffix: plan_answer.\n204\tPROCESS-TREE prompt (D18 \"child claiming a parent it never had\"): flavour unless asked/telemetry ships. Then lib.codec:\n205\t declared_spawns(plans, srcs) vs process_events(bytes) -> process_tree -> reconcile_processes(...) -> reconcile_processes_answer\n206\t (liar = recorded parent != declared parent, PPID spoofing T1134.004; GUID before pid; original spelling).\n207\tATT&CK when no attack= in plan: role table in lib.scripts.role_attack; host-language sub-ids T1059.001 PS .002 AppleScript\n208\t .003 cmd .004 unix shell .005 VB .006 python .007 JS .010 AutoHotKey/AutoIt .011 Lua; v=3 used parent T1059 (C#/Groovy/GHA).\n209\tCI/PERSISTENCE prompt (D21 \"trigger, trust boundary, job that keeps coming back\"): flavour unless asked; then GAP rows 78/79.\n210\t```\n211\t\n212\t## Readiness gaps\n213\tBuilt by the nightly prebuild (dropped from the queue, still usable from lib/): D16-D19 nights (see git history) and D20 night\n214\tpipeline-step-inner-scripts (`pipeline_steps`), prior-language-host-battery, jvm-dsl-script-route, groovy-literal-fold,\n215\tnotebook-manifest-json-carrier (`json_scripts`), pipeline-execution-locus (`execution_locus`/`locus_answer`),\n216\tcompiled-lang-source-route, jenkins-artifact-secrets, evidence-magic-classifier (`evidence_kind`). Given up (2 attempts):\n217\tpython-exec-onion-static, evidence-type-router, file-registry-telemetry-reconcile. build-manifest-hooks failed once (retry\n218\tqueued). Prebuild gate: lib imports limited to hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS (stdlib parsers + Crypto/cryptography/dpkt/\n219\tEvtx/pefile/olefile/dnfile; no csv/ast/shlex/marshal). Priority-1 order for D22: the D21 theme the bytes did not carry yet\n220\t(GHA trigger/trust model, schedule persistence), the next CI YAML sibling, GitHub action/reusable-workflow handoffs; then\n221\tinjection/secrets, k8s/IaC carriers, YAML carrier twists, repo hooks, launchd.\n222\t\n223\t```json\n224\t[\n225\t  {\"id\": \"gha-trigger-trust-model\", \"concept\": \"GitHub Actions trigger / permission / runner trust-boundary model (who can trigger a workflow, which runner and token inherit the trust)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D21 prompt: 'decides who can trigger it and which runner inherits the trust. Identify each trigger and trust boundary'. D21 bytes were all `on: workflow_dispatch:` + `runs-on: ubuntu-latest`, so a variant/next day adding real triggers would ask new suffixes (`-trigger`, `-runner`, `-trust-boundary`, `-permissions`). Build gha_workflow(name, src)->{name, triggers:[event names incl. filters], jobs:[{id, runs_on, self_hosted(bool), container, environment, permissions (workflow- and job-level, 'write-all'/'read-all'/map), needs, if, steps:[{name, uses, run, shell, with, env}]}], secrets_used, untrusted_contexts} with a regex/indent YAML walk (reuse lib.codec _yaml_* helpers; PyYAML 1.1 turns `on:` into True -- accept both `on`/`'on'`/`true` keys if a parser is used). Trust labels: privileged-trigger set {pull_request_target, workflow_run, issue_comment, issues, discussion*, fork PR via pull_request_target + checkout of `github.event.pull_request.head.(sha|ref)`}, runner trust {github-hosted, self-hosted (any label list containing self-hosted), container}, token scope (none/read/write per key). gha_answer(model, field, accepted_values, what=) maps to enums by original spelling. Gate: synthetic workflows covering each trigger form (`on: push`, `on: [push, pull_request]`, map with filters, `schedule`, `workflow_call`) + the D21 members (triggers=['workflow_dispatch'], runner github-hosted).\"},\n226\t  {\"id\": \"ci-schedule-persistence-model\", \"concept\": \"'the job that keeps coming back': schedule / re-trigger persistence across CI, OS and orchestrator descriptors\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D21 base id `github-actions-persistence` + prompt 'find the job that keeps coming back' -- not in the bytes yet. schedule_entries(name, src)->[{kind, expr, period_s (best effort), target(job/command), lang, attack}] for GHA `on: schedule: - cron: '..'` (5-field POSIX cron, UTC), `workflow_run: workflows: [..] types: [completed]` self/cyclic chains (graph cycle = keeps coming back), `repository_dispatch` + a step that calls the dispatches API, GitLab `rules: - if: '$CI_PIPELINE_SOURCE == \\\"schedule\\\"'`, Azure `schedules: - cron:`, K8s `kind: CronJob spec.schedule`, systemd `.timer` OnCalendar/OnBootSec/OnUnitActiveSec + `Restart=always`, crontab/`/etc/cron.d` lines incl. `@reboot`, launchd plist StartInterval/StartCalendarInterval/RunAtLoad/KeepAlive, Task Scheduler XML triggers (TimeTrigger Repetition Interval PT5M, LogonTrigger, BootTrigger), WMI __IntervalTimerInstruction/__EventFilter WITHIN n, Run/RunOnce keys. ATT&CK: T1053.003 cron, .005 schtasks, .006 systemd timers, .007 container orchestration job, T1543.001 launch agent/.002 systemd service/.004 launch daemon, T1546.003 WMI, T1547.001 Run keys; CI persistence via workflow file = T1098/T1195.002 hint only. persistence_answer(entries, field, accepted_values). Gate: fixtures per kind + every D1-D21 member returns [].\"},\n227\t  {\"id\": \"ci-yaml-sibling-route\", \"concept\": \"next CI YAML languages after D21 GitHub Actions: GitLab CI, Azure Pipelines, CircleCI, Bitbucket, Drone, Buildkite, Tekton\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D20 Jenkins -> D21 GHA; the CI sibling is the likeliest next language. Verify lib.codec.v3_plan/find_codecs + pipeline_steps on a fixture battery wrapping D21 plans: GitLab `.gitlab-ci.yml` (`variables: HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR: \\\"..\\\"` top-level or per-job, `script:`/`before_script:` lists, `include:`, `extends:`, `!reference [..]`), Azure `azure-pipelines.yml` (`variables: - name: X value: ..` list form AND map form, `- script:`/`- bash:`/`- powershell:`/`- pwsh:`/`- task: PowerShell@2 inputs: script:`), CircleCI (`environment:`, `run: command: |`, orbs), Bitbucket (`pipelines: default: - step: script:`), Drone (`commands:`), Buildkite (`command:`), Tekton (`steps[].script:`). Descriptor may be UPPERCASE without an id (D21 HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR) -- accept `HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR(_\\\\w+)?` and `descriptor_\\\\w+` keys in env/variables/environment maps. Family guesses `polyglot-gitlab_ci`, `polyglot-azure_pipelines`, `polyglot-circleci`. Gate: D1-D21 members unchanged.\"},\n228\t  {\"id\": \"github-action-definition-route\", \"concept\": \"GitHub action definitions and reusable workflows as the 'static handoff into the next language'\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D21 prompt: 'follow the static handoff into the next language'. action_handoffs(members: {name: text})->[{from, via, to_lang, body_or_target}]: `action.yml`/`action.yaml` `runs: using: composite` (steps run+shell), `using: node16|node20|node24` + `main:`/`pre:`/`post:` JS entry (resolve to a member, route as JS/TS), `using: docker` + `image: Dockerfile|docker://` + `entrypoint:`/`args:` (route Dockerfile via lib.codec Docker route); workflows `uses: ./.github/actions/x` (local, resolve), `uses: owner/repo/.github/workflows/x.yml@ref` (`on: workflow_call` reusable, `inputs:`/`secrets: inherit`), `uses: actions/github-script@v7` `with: script: |` (JS body), `run:` with `shell: bash|pwsh|powershell|python|cmd|sh` or custom `shell: perl {0}` -> language. Map to next_language spellings used by v=3 plans (powershell, jscript/node, batch, vbscript, python, bash). Gate: synthetic repo trees + D21 members (no handoff, only `run: ':'`).\"},\n229\t  {\"id\": \"build-manifest-hooks\", \"concept\": \"package/build lifecycle hooks as script hosts (supply-chain sibling of Jenkins)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"install-time execution surfaces: npm `package.json` lifecycle scripts + `binding.gyp` actions; Python `setup.py` `cmdclass={'install': ..}` / `pyproject.toml` `[tool.setuptools]` / `.pth` files with `import` lines; Ruby `.gemspec` `extensions` + `extconf.rb`; Rust `build.rs`; Go `//go:generate`; Maven `pom.xml` `exec-maven-plugin` `<executable>`/`<arguments>` + `maven-antrun-plugin` `<exec>`; Gradle `exec {}`; MSBuild `.csproj` `<Target BeforeTargets=..><Exec Command=..>`; NuGet `tools/install.ps1`; Makefile/CMake `execute_process`. hooks(name, src)->[{hook, when (install|build|test|import), command, lang}] + ATT&CK hints (T1195.001/.002 supply chain, T1059.x by lang). Gate: battery wrapping D1-D21 plans; D1-D21 unchanged. (Retry after 1 failed attempt on D20 night: keep the scope to manifest parsing + hook listing; reuse json_scripts/pipeline_steps rather than new parsers.)\"},\n230\t  {\"id\": \"ci-expression-injection-secrets\", \"concept\": \"GitHub/GitLab expression contexts: untrusted input interpolated into run bodies, secrets/token exposure\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Trust-boundary questions may ask which step is injectable or which secret leaks. ci_expressions(src)->[{job, step, field, expr, context_root, untrusted(bool), sink (run/script/with.script/env)}] over `${{ .. }}` (GHA) and `$VAR`/`${VAR}` + `$CI_*` (GitLab): untrusted roots github.event.(issue|pull_request|comment|review|review_comment|discussion|pages|commits|head_commit).*(title|body|name|message|label|ref|email|default_branch|head_ref), github.head_ref; secrets.*, GITHUB_TOKEN, ACTIONS_ID_TOKEN_REQUEST_*, `echo \\\"::add-mask::\\\"`, writes to $GITHUB_ENV/$GITHUB_OUTPUT/$GITHUB_PATH (env injection), `pull_request_target` + checkout + run (pwn request). ATT&CK hints T1059.004 injection sink, T1552.001/.004/.007, T1528. Gate: fixtures with known injectable steps; D21 members -> [].\"},\n231\t  {\"id\": \"k8s-helm-manifest-route\", \"concept\": \"Kubernetes / Helm / Kustomize manifests carrying scripts (CronJob, Job, DaemonSet, ConfigMap, Secret)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Orchestration sibling of CI YAML and the cleanest 'keeps coming back' carrier (T1053.007). k8s_scripts(name, src)->[{doc_index, kind, name, container, command, args, script_lang, schedule}] over multi-doc `---`: `spec.(template.)spec.containers[].command/args` (`[\\\"/bin/sh\\\",\\\"-c\\\",\\\"..\\\"]` flow or block lists), `jobTemplate` for CronJob + `spec.schedule`, ConfigMap `data:` script blocks (`|`), Secret `data:` base64 (decode) / `stringData:`, `initContainers`, `lifecycle.postStart.exec.command`, hostPath/privileged flags (trust boundary). Helm: strip `{{ .. }}`/`{{- .. -}}`, fold `{{ \\\"..\\\" | b64dec }}` / `b64enc` over literals, `.Values` lookups from a values.yaml member. Then v3_plan/find_codecs per body. Gate: fixtures wrapping D21 plans; D1-D21 unchanged.\"},\n232\t  {\"id\": \"cloud-iac-userdata-route\", \"concept\": \"IaC templates with embedded scripts: Terraform local-exec/user_data, CloudFormation UserData Fn::Base64, ARM/Bicep deploymentScripts, Ansible shell tasks\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"After CI, infra-as-code is the next 'build that runs code' surface. iac_scripts(name, src)->[{resource, field, lang, body}]: Terraform HCL `provisioner \\\"local-exec\\\" { command = <<-EOT .. EOT interpreter = [\\\"pwsh\\\",\\\"-c\\\"] }`, `user_data = base64encode(..)`/`filebase64(..)`/`templatefile`, `data \\\"external\\\" { program = [..] }`; CloudFormation YAML/JSON `UserData: Fn::Base64: !Sub |` (short-form tags `!Sub`/`!Join`/`!Base64` -- tag-tolerant walk), `AWS::SSM::Document` `runCommand`; ARM JSON `Microsoft.Resources/deploymentScripts` `properties.scriptContent` + `kind: AzurePowerShell|AzureCLI`, Bicep `scriptContent: '''..'''`; Ansible `ansible.builtin.shell/command/script/raw/win_shell` (`args: executable:`), `become:`. Heredoc/`'''` joins, `${var}` interpolation left as-is. Gate: fixtures wrapping D21 plans; D1-D21 unchanged.\"},\n233\t  {\"id\": \"yaml-scalar-carrier-twists\", \"concept\": \"YAML-specific carrier mutations for the D21 language: block/folded scalars, anchors/aliases, tags, escapes, multi-doc\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D21 carriers were a one-line quoted scalar; the next twist on a YAML language (as D18/D19 twisted theirs) would hide the descriptor in YAML semantics. yaml_scalar(src, key)->decoded text honoring: literal `|`/`|-`/`|+` (keep newlines) vs folded `>`/`>-` (lines JOIN WITH A SPACE -- strip spaces before peeling hex/base64), indentation indicators `|2`, double-quoted escapes (`\\\\x41` `\\\\u0041` `\\\\U..` `\\\\n`, line-folding with trailing `\\\\`), single-quoted `''`, plain multi-line scalars, anchors `&d` + aliases `*d` + merge keys `<<: *base` (descriptor defined in one job, used in another), `!!binary` (base64 -> bytes), `!!str`, flow maps/sequences `{X: \\\"..\\\"}`/`[\\\"a\\\",\\\"b\\\"]` with a join step, comments after values, multi-document `---`/`...`, CRLF. Also the marker split across several `#` comment lines. Gate: each twist applied to the D21 members peels back to the same plan; D1-D21 unchanged.\"},\n234\t  {\"id\": \"solver-lib-v3-fallback\", \"concept\": \"carried solve.py must ask lib.codec.v3_plan when its own v=3 read yields nothing\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D19: lib.codec.v3_plan already decoded the ASPX escaped-nested carrier, but the carried solve.py `_v3` only used its own V3_MARK/descriptor regexes, so 11 ids went planless and the race harness probed guesses. The D20 solver-authoring pass: in analyse_v3, if no candidate peels to `v=`, call lib.codec.v3_plan(text) (and lib.codec.find_codecs) before giving up; log which reader won. Same for D18 SPLIT (now in both). STILL OPEN after D21: the D21 solve.py has no lib.codec.v3_plan / inner_scripts call (D20-D21 needed none because every carrier was plain). Do it in the next solver-authoring pass.\"},\n235\t  {\"id\": \"php-cli\", \"concept\": \"PHP CLI for lint/tokenize\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y php-cli  (php -l, token_get_all; never run fixtures). PHP is a carried language since D8.\"},\n236\t  {\"id\": \"lua-unluac\", \"concept\": \"Lua interpreter + bytecode decompiler\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y lua5.4 luajit ; unluac.jar from https://sourceforge.net/projects/unluac/ into tools/unluac (java 25 installed) with bin/unluac wrapper. Needed if a luac-compiled carrier variant of the D9 Lua fixtures appears.\"},\n237\t  {\"id\": \"xsltproc-cabextract-yq\", \"concept\": \"XML/CAB/YAML helpers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y xsltproc cabextract ; yq: pip install yq into .venv (jq wrapper; jq installed). xsltproc only for --noout lint, never to apply a stylesheet.\"},\n238\t  {\"id\": \"leaf-ext-list\", \"concept\": \"nested-zip sniff skips unknown leaf extensions\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"_LEAF_EXT in solve.py still lacks .lua .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb .ahk .gs .csx .groovy .yml (and future .tcl .r .kts .java .jsp .ipynb .go .rs .awk .tf .xsl .reg .inf). Speed only (~1 s); prefer sniffing PK magic over an extension list.\"},\n239\t  {\"id\": \"new-synthetic-label-family\", \"concept\": \"code-shape labels for a new language (D2-D7 style)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Polyglot days have been plan-verbatim since D8, but an 'advanced <lang>' set (like bash-advanced) would bring feature/primitive or control/style labels, and OLD label families can flip regime (batch expansion D15/D16). Apply playbook NAMING LAWS; probe one field per submit; check started_at/run_for_time first.\"},\n240\t  {\"id\": \"family-name-underscore\", \"concept\": \"host-type families like polyglot-github_actions / host-<profile>-<lang>\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Keep the longest-known-suffix field parse; derive the family prefix from the contract ids, never from the file stem (D14 msbuild_xml). D17 added `polyglot-auto_hotkey` (campaign AUTO_HOTKEY-, url host auto_hotkey-..). D18: `polyglot-google_apps_script` (campaign GOOGLE_APPS_SCRIPT-, url host google_apps_script-..) while its host file is hyphenated `host-google-docs-sidebar-google-apps-script` (profile google_docs_sidebar). D19: `polyglot-csharp_script` (campaign CSHARP_SCRIPT-, url host csharp_script-..) and host `host-aspx-inline-csharp-csharp-script` (profile aspx_inline_csharp, file extension .csx although the bytes are an ASPX page). D20: `polyglot-groovy` (campaign GROOVY-), hosts `host-jenkins-pipeline-groovy` (profile jenkins_pipeline) and `host-classic-asp-vbscript` (profile classic_asp, language vbscript, campaign VBSCRIPT-, file .vbs although the bytes are an ASP page). D21: `polyglot-github_actions` (campaign GITHUB_ACTIONS-, url host github_actions-.., file_path /tmp/huntress-github_actions/..), no host file.\"},\n241\t  {\"id\": \"tcl-r-interpreters\", \"concept\": \"tclsh / Rscript for syntax checks\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y tcl (small); r-base-core is ~100 MB, install only on an R day. Static reading is enough for v=3 plans.\"},\n242\t  {\"id\": \"applescript-scpt\", \"concept\": \"compiled AppleScript (.scpt FasdUAS) disassembly\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Jinmo/applescript-disassembler into tools/ (pure python). D13 shipped source .applescript only; a compiled variant would hide the marker in UTF-16/MacRoman strings.\"},\n243\t  {\"id\": \"js-deob-extras\", \"concept\": \"synchrony / JSFuck decoding\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"npm i deobfuscator (synchrony CLI) into tools/npm; webcrack (installed) already handles obfuscator.io; JSFuck/JJencode via js_sandbox capture of the final call.\"},\n244\t  {\"id\": \"ps-deob-modules\", \"concept\": \"PowerDecode / PSDecode for pwsh\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Malandrone/PowerDecode and https://github.com/R3MRUM/PSDecode into tools/ (pwsh 7.6.6 installed). refinery ps1 covers most; these add layer-by-layer IEX override tracing.\"},\n245\t  {\"id\": \"xlm-standalone\", \"concept\": \"XLMMacroDeobfuscator CLI\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python XLMMacroDeobfuscator  (refinery xlmdeobf is an inlined port and already works; standalone gives --sort-formulas/--extract-only).\"},\n246\t  {\"id\": \"dotnet-script\", \"concept\": \"csx inspection\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D19 shipped .csx source only (static read was enough). Install dotnet-script only if a csx variant needs `#load`/`#r` resolution: dotnet tool install --tool-path tools/dotnet-tools dotnet-script (parse only; ilspycmd covers compiled InstallUtil/MSBuild/Assembly.Load payloads).\"},\n247\t  {\"id\": \"git-repo-hooks-route\", \"concept\": \"repository-level auto-run surfaces: git hooks, filter/diff drivers, husky, pre-commit, devcontainer, submodules\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Supply-chain persistence next to CI: repo_hooks(members)->[{surface, trigger, command, lang}]: `.git/hooks/{pre-commit,post-checkout,post-merge,pre-push}` (shebang -> lang), `.git/config` `[core] hooksPath`, `[filter \\\"x\\\"] clean/smudge = ..` + `.gitattributes` `* filter=x`, `[diff \\\"x\\\"] textconv`, `[core] fsmonitor = ..`, `.husky/*`, `.pre-commit-config.yaml` `repos[].hooks[].entry` + `language:`, `.gitmodules` url/update=!cmd, `.devcontainer/devcontainer.json` postCreate/postStart (reuse json_scripts), `.vscode/tasks.json` `runOn: folderOpen`. ATT&CK hints T1195.002, T1546 (event-triggered), T1059.x. Gate: synthetic repo fixtures; D1-D21 unchanged.\"},\n248\t  {\"id\": \"launchd-plist-route\", \"concept\": \"macOS launchd / plist persistence (XML and binary plist)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"OS-side 'keeps coming back' sibling of D13 AppleScript. plist_scripts(name, data)->[{label, program_arguments, run_at_load, keep_alive, start_interval, lang}] for XML plists (`<key>ProgramArguments</key><array><string>/bin/sh</string><string>-c</string><string>..</string>`) and binary `bplist00` (pure-Python parser: offset table, object refs; ints, strings ASCII/UTF-16BE, arrays, dicts, data, bools), `LaunchAgents`/`LaunchDaemons` path hints, `osascript -e` bodies -> AppleScript route. ATT&CK T1543.001/.004, T1647. Gate: plistlib-generated XML+binary fixtures round-trip (plistlib is stdlib; check ALLOWED_IMPORTS, else hand-parse).\"}\n249\t]\n250\t```\n251\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d9e4c1fd-64ee-40f8-9d13-bc0ad5c50086","uuid":"6d3473d0-3bd1-47c7-8f59-25c9ca99276d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:10:39.805Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/script-analysis.md","content":" marker data running into `\\n..` / descriptor `= \\\"..\\\"` (D19 ASPX: inner script is an ESCAPED string) -> unescape `\\n \\\" \\\\`\n   (`\"\"`, `&quot;`, CDATA, `\\u0022`) and rescan. A v=3 file with no plan = CARRIER bug: call lib.codec.v3_plan(text) first\n   (it read D18 + D19), then fix the read -- never walk role/attack enums or put a guessed value in a bulk POST.\n descriptor syntaxes to accept: `x = \"..\"` `x := \"..\"` `set x \"..\"`/`set x {..}` `x <- \"..\"` `X: &str = \"..\"`\n   `DESCRIPTOR_X = \"..\"` (Ruby const, seen D16) `descriptor_x: \"..\"` (YAML) `<HuntressDescriptor>..</..>` (XML) heredoc/block scalar\n material may wrap (`|` YAML, `=begin`, `<# #>`, `\"\"\"`, `\\`, `.`/`+`/`&`/`..` concat): join pieces, strip separators, THEN peel\n peel by SHAPE, max 4 layers, accept only output starting `v=` (or `{` JSON): hex (any separators) | base64 std/urlsafe\n   (also reversed text) | base32 [A-Z2-7=] | base85/ascii85 <~~> | gzip H4sI / zlib eJ eN eF | rot13 | %xx | \\xNN \\NNN \\ddd\n   \\uXXXX \\u{..} | int lists (READ the radix from code) | UTF-16LE inside b64 (PS -enc: every 2nd byte 00)\n copy plan values verbatim (role, attack, adapter, steps, profiles, next_language); never derive them from code\nLAYERED OBFUSCATION -> standard tool (static, no network, no exec of behaviour):\n PowerShell   .venv/bin/ps1 < f  (folds -f reorder, `ticks, 'a'+'b', [char]N, -join, -replace, .Invoke)\n JS           webcrack f.js -o out/  (obfuscator.io arrays) | .venv/bin/js < f | node hctf/js_sandbox.js f (eval->capture)\n VBA/VBS      .venv/bin/olevba --decode --deobf f | .venv/bin/vba < f.bas | pcodedmp f.doc (stomped p-code)\n Batch        .venv/bin/bat < f  (emulates set/%x:~a,b%/%x:a=b%/^/delayed !x!; prints commands, runs nothing)\n XLM .venv/bin/xlmdeobf | OneNote xtone -l | CHM xtchm -l | LNK .venv/bin/lnk | AutoIt autoit-ripper x.exe out/, a3x\n Python       swap exec/eval->print, run with python3 -I in an empty dir; marshal blob -> pycdc / xdis (match version)\n compressed   .venv/bin/b64 < blob | .venv/bin/decompress   (gzip/zlib/raw deflate/lzma/bz2 auto)\n PHP chains   apply the named functions innermost-first in Python (base64_decode, gzinflate=raw deflate, str_rot13, strrev)\nNEVER: run the fixture's interpreter on the file (ruby/perl/php/tclsh/Rscript/make/go run/msbuild/pwsh -File);\n `perl -MO=Deparse` and `make -n` still execute BEGIN/$(shell) -> strip first; apply XSLT; open URLs from the plan.\nSYNTHETIC LABELS (if a new language brings code-shape questions): read accepted_values; compose `<keyword>_guard`,\n `<keyword>_once`, `<keyword>_<action>`. Batch `expansion` = STATEMENT-ONLY table by default (D15+); a carried label rejected\n on unchanged bytes = GM regime moved: tabulate (construct, label) vs started_at/run_for_time/variant_fresh first.\nEQUIVALENCE/OUTLIER prompt (D16): only if asked; compare lib.codec.plan_canonical (role/steps/adapter/attack/profiles).\nNETWORK-RECONCILE prompt (D17 \"source vs network evidence, indicator on one side\"): flavour unless a question/net file exists;\n then lib.codec.network_indicators(bytes) (pcap/HAR/Zeek/Sysmon 3,22) + reconcile({member: plan}, bytes) -> reconcile_answer\n (r, kind, accepted, what=). Graph ids: download_graph(plans) -> download_graph_answer. Unknown plan-key suffix: plan_answer.\nPROCESS-TREE prompt (D18 \"child claiming a parent it never had\"): flavour unless asked/telemetry ships. Then lib.codec:\n declared_spawns(plans, srcs) vs process_events(bytes) -> process_tree -> reconcile_processes(...) -> reconcile_processes_answer\n (liar = recorded parent != declared parent, PPID spoofing T1134.004; GUID before pid; original spelling).\nATT&CK when no attack= in plan: role table in lib.scripts.role_attack; host-language sub-ids T1059.001 PS .002 AppleScript\n .003 cmd .004 unix shell .005 VB .006 python .007 JS .010 AutoHotKey/AutoIt .011 Lua; v=3 used parent T1059 (C#/Groovy/GHA).\nCI/PERSISTENCE prompt (D21 \"trigger, trust boundary, job that keeps coming back\"): flavour unless asked; then GAP rows 78/79.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\nBuilt by the nightly prebuild (dropped from the queue, still usable from lib/): D16-D19 nights (see git history) and D20 night\npipeline-step-inner-scripts (`pipeline_steps`), prior-language-host-battery, jvm-dsl-script-route, groovy-literal-fold,\nnotebook-manifest-json-carrier (`json_scripts`), pipeline-execution-locus (`execution_locus`/`locus_answer`),\ncompiled-lang-source-route, jenkins-artifact-secrets, evidence-magic-classifier (`evidence_kind`). Given up (2 attempts):\npython-exec-onion-static, evidence-type-router, file-registry-telemetry-reconcile. build-manifest-hooks failed once (retry\nqueued). Prebuild gate: lib imports limited to hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS (stdlib parsers + Crypto/cryptography/dpkt/\nEvtx/pefile/olefile/dnfile; no csv/ast/shlex/marshal). Priority-1 order for D22: the D21 theme the bytes did not carry yet\n(GHA trigger/trust model, schedule persistence), the next CI YAML sibling, GitHub action/reusable-workflow handoffs; then\ninjection/secrets, k8s/IaC carriers, YAML carrier twists, repo hooks, launchd.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"gha-trigger-trust-model\", \"concept\": \"GitHub Actions trigger / permission / runner trust-boundary model (who can trigger a workflow, which runner and token inherit the trust)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D21 prompt: 'decides who can trigger it and which runner inherits the trust. Identify each trigger and trust boundary'. D21 bytes were all `on: workflow_dispatch:` + `runs-on: ubuntu-latest`, so a variant/next day adding real triggers would ask new suffixes (`-trigger`, `-runner`, `-trust-boundary`, `-permissions`). Build gha_workflow(name, src)->{name, triggers:[event names incl. filters], jobs:[{id, runs_on, self_hosted(bool), container, environment, permissions (workflow- and job-level, 'write-all'/'read-all'/map), needs, if, steps:[{name, uses, run, shell, with, env}]}], secrets_used, untrusted_contexts} with a regex/indent YAML walk (reuse lib.codec _yaml_* helpers; PyYAML 1.1 turns `on:` into True -- accept both `on`/`'on'`/`true` keys if a parser is used). Trust labels: privileged-trigger set {pull_request_target, workflow_run, issue_comment, issues, discussion*, fork PR via pull_request_target + checkout of `github.event.pull_request.head.(sha|ref)`}, runner trust {github-hosted, self-hosted (any label list containing self-hosted), container}, token scope (none/read/write per key). gha_answer(model, field, accepted_values, what=) maps to enums by original spelling. Gate: synthetic workflows covering each trigger form (`on: push`, `on: [push, pull_request]`, map with filters, `schedule`, `workflow_call`) + the D21 members (triggers=['workflow_dispatch'], runner github-hosted).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ci-schedule-persistence-model\", \"concept\": \"'the job that keeps coming back': schedule / re-trigger persistence across CI, OS and orchestrator descriptors\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D21 base id `github-actions-persistence` + prompt 'find the job that keeps coming back' -- not in the bytes yet. schedule_entries(name, src)->[{kind, expr, period_s (best effort), target(job/command), lang, attack}] for GHA `on: schedule: - cron: '..'` (5-field POSIX cron, UTC), `workflow_run: workflows: [..] types: [completed]` self/cyclic chains (graph cycle = keeps coming back), `repository_dispatch` + a step that calls the dispatches API, GitLab `rules: - if: '$CI_PIPELINE_SOURCE == \\\"schedule\\\"'`, Azure `schedules: - cron:`, K8s `kind: CronJob spec.schedule`, systemd `.timer` OnCalendar/OnBootSec/OnUnitActiveSec + `Restart=always`, crontab/`/etc/cron.d` lines incl. `@reboot`, launchd plist StartInterval/StartCalendarInterval/RunAtLoad/KeepAlive, Task Scheduler XML triggers (TimeTrigger Repetition Interval PT5M, LogonTrigger, BootTrigger), WMI __IntervalTimerInstruction/__EventFilter WITHIN n, Run/RunOnce keys. ATT&CK: T1053.003 cron, .005 schtasks, .006 systemd timers, .007 container orchestration job, T1543.001 launch agent/.002 systemd service/.004 launch daemon, T1546.003 WMI, T1547.001 Run keys; CI persistence via workflow file = T1098/T1195.002 hint only. persistence_answer(entries, field, accepted_values). Gate: fixtures per kind + every D1-D21 member returns [].\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ci-yaml-sibling-route\", \"concept\": \"next CI YAML languages after D21 GitHub Actions: GitLab CI, Azure Pipelines, CircleCI, Bitbucket, Drone, Buildkite, Tekton\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D20 Jenkins -> D21 GHA; the CI sibling is the likeliest next language. Verify lib.codec.v3_plan/find_codecs + pipeline_steps on a fixture battery wrapping D21 plans: GitLab `.gitlab-ci.yml` (`variables: HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR: \\\"..\\\"` top-level or per-job, `script:`/`before_script:` lists, `include:`, `extends:`, `!reference [..]`), Azure `azure-pipelines.yml` (`variables: - name: X value: ..` list form AND map form, `- script:`/`- bash:`/`- powershell:`/`- pwsh:`/`- task: PowerShell@2 inputs: script:`), CircleCI (`environment:`, `run: command: |`, orbs), Bitbucket (`pipelines: default: - step: script:`), Drone (`commands:`), Buildkite (`command:`), Tekton (`steps[].script:`). Descriptor may be UPPERCASE without an id (D21 HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR) -- accept `HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR(_\\\\w+)?` and `descriptor_\\\\w+` keys in env/variables/environment maps. Family guesses `polyglot-gitlab_ci`, `polyglot-azure_pipelines`, `polyglot-circleci`. Gate: D1-D21 members unchanged.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"github-action-definition-route\", \"concept\": \"GitHub action definitions and reusable workflows as the 'static handoff into the next language'\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D21 prompt: 'follow the static handoff into the next language'. action_handoffs(members: {name: text})->[{from, via, to_lang, body_or_target}]: `action.yml`/`action.yaml` `runs: using: composite` (steps run+shell), `using: node16|node20|node24` + `main:`/`pre:`/`post:` JS entry (resolve to a member, route as JS/TS), `using: docker` + `image: Dockerfile|docker://` + `entrypoint:`/`args:` (route Dockerfile via lib.codec Docker route); workflows `uses: ./.github/actions/x` (local, resolve), `uses: owner/repo/.github/workflows/x.yml@ref` (`on: workflow_call` reusable, `inputs:`/`secrets: inherit`), `uses: actions/github-script@v7` `with: script: |` (JS body), `run:` with `shell: bash|pwsh|powershell|python|cmd|sh` or custom `shell: perl {0}` -> language. Map to next_language spellings used by v=3 plans (powershell, jscript/node, batch, vbscript, python, bash). Gate: synthetic repo trees + D21 members (no handoff, only `run: ':'`).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"build-manifest-hooks\", \"concept\": \"package/build lifecycle hooks as script hosts (supply-chain sibling of Jenkins)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"install-time execution surfaces: npm `package.json` lifecycle scripts + `binding.gyp` actions; Python `setup.py` `cmdclass={'install': ..}` / `pyproject.toml` `[tool.setuptools]` / `.pth` files with `import` lines; Ruby `.gemspec` `extensions` + `extconf.rb`; Rust `build.rs`; Go `//go:generate`; Maven `pom.xml` `exec-maven-plugin` `<executable>`/`<arguments>` + `maven-antrun-plugin` `<exec>`; Gradle `exec {}`; MSBuild `.csproj` `<Target BeforeTargets=..><Exec Command=..>`; NuGet `tools/install.ps1`; Makefile/CMake `execute_process`. hooks(name, src)->[{hook, when (install|build|test|import), command, lang}] + ATT&CK hints (T1195.001/.002 supply chain, T1059.x by lang). Gate: battery wrapping D1-D21 plans; D1-D21 unchanged. (Retry after 1 failed attempt on D20 night: keep the scope to manifest parsing + hook listing; reuse json_scripts/pipeline_steps rather than new parsers.)\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ci-expression-injection-secrets\", \"concept\": \"GitHub/GitLab expression contexts: untrusted input interpolated into run bodies, secrets/token exposure\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Trust-boundary questions may ask which step is injectable or which secret leaks. ci_expressions(src)->[{job, step, field, expr, context_root, untrusted(bool), sink (run/script/with.script/env)}] over `${{ .. }}` (GHA) and `$VAR`/`${VAR}` + `$CI_*` (GitLab): untrusted roots github.event.(issue|pull_request|comment|review|review_comment|discussion|pages|commits|head_commit).*(title|body|name|message|label|ref|email|default_branch|head_ref), github.head_ref; secrets.*, GITHUB_TOKEN, ACTIONS_ID_TOKEN_REQUEST_*, `echo \\\"::add-mask::\\\"`, writes to $GITHUB_ENV/$GITHUB_OUTPUT/$GITHUB_PATH (env injection), `pull_request_target` + checkout + run (pwn request). ATT&CK hints T1059.004 injection sink, T1552.001/.004/.007, T1528. Gate: fixtures with known injectable steps; D21 members -> [].\"},\n  {\"id\": \"k8s-helm-manifest-route\", \"concept\": \"Kubernetes / Helm / Kustomize manifests carrying scripts (CronJob, Job, DaemonSet, ConfigMap, Secret)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Orchestration sibling of CI YAML and the cleanest 'keeps coming back' carrier (T1053.007). k8s_scripts(name, src)->[{doc_index, kind, name, container, command, args, script_lang, schedule}] over multi-doc `---`: `spec.(template.)spec.containers[].command/args` (`[\\\"/bin/sh\\\",\\\"-c\\\",\\\"..\\\"]` flow or block lists), `jobTemplate` for CronJob + `spec.schedule`, ConfigMap `data:` script blocks (`|`), Secret `data:` base64 (decode) / `stringData:`, `initContainers`, `lifecycle.postStart.exec.command`, hostPath/privileged flags (trust boundary). Helm: strip `{{ .. }}`/`{{- .. -}}`, fold `{{ \\\"..\\\" | b64dec }}` / `b64enc` over literals, `.Values` lookups from a values.yaml member. Then v3_plan/find_codecs per body. Gate: fixtures wrapping D21 plans; D1-D21 unchanged.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cloud-iac-userdata-route\", \"concept\": \"IaC templates with embedded scripts: Terraform local-exec/user_data, CloudFormation UserData Fn::Base64, ARM/Bicep deploymentScripts, Ansible shell tasks\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"After CI, infra-as-code is the next 'build that runs code' surface. iac_scripts(name, src)->[{resource, field, lang, body}]: Terraform HCL `provisioner \\\"local-exec\\\" { command = <<-EOT .. EOT interpreter = [\\\"pwsh\\\",\\\"-c\\\"] }`, `user_data = base64encode(..)`/`filebase64(..)`/`templatefile`, `data \\\"external\\\" { program = [..] }`; CloudFormation YAML/JSON `UserData: Fn::Base64: !Sub |` (short-form tags `!Sub`/`!Join`/`!Base64` -- tag-tolerant walk), `AWS::SSM::Document` `runCommand`; ARM JSON `Microsoft.Resources/deploymentScripts` `properties.scriptContent` + `kind: AzurePowerShell|AzureCLI`, Bicep `scriptContent: '''..'''`; Ansible `ansible.builtin.shell/command/script/raw/win_shell` (`args: executable:`), `become:`. Heredoc/`'''` joins, `${var}` interpolation left as-is. Gate: fixtures wrapping D21 plans; D1-D21 unchanged.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"yaml-scalar-carrier-twists\", \"concept\": \"YAML-specific carrier mutations for the D21 language: block/folded scalars, anchors/aliases, tags, escapes, multi-doc\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D21 carriers were a one-line quoted scalar; the next twist on a YAML language (as D18/D19 twisted theirs) would hide the descriptor in YAML semantics. yaml_scalar(src, key)->decoded text honoring: literal `|`/`|-`/`|+` (keep newlines) vs folded `>`/`>-` (lines JOIN WITH A SPACE -- strip spaces before peeling hex/base64), indentation indicators `|2`, double-quoted escapes (`\\\\x41` `\\\\u0041` `\\\\U..` `\\\\n`, line-folding with trailing `\\\\`), single-quoted `''`, plain multi-line scalars, anchors `&d` + aliases `*d` + merge keys `<<: *base` (descriptor defined in one job, used in another), `!!binary` (base64 -> bytes), `!!str`, flow maps/sequences `{X: \\\"..\\\"}`/`[\\\"a\\\",\\\"b\\\"]` with a join step, comments after values, multi-document `---`/`...`, CRLF. Also the marker split across several `#` comment lines. Gate: each twist applied to the D21 members peels back to the same plan; D1-D21 unchanged.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"solver-lib-v3-fallback\", \"concept\": \"carried solve.py must ask lib.codec.v3_plan when its own v=3 read yields nothing\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D19: lib.codec.v3_plan already decoded the ASPX escaped-nested carrier, but the carried solve.py `_v3` only used its own V3_MARK/descriptor regexes, so 11 ids went planless and the race harness probed guesses. The D20 solver-authoring pass: in analyse_v3, if no candidate peels to `v=`, call lib.codec.v3_plan(text) (and lib.codec.find_codecs) before giving up; log which reader won. Same for D18 SPLIT (now in both). STILL OPEN after D21: the D21 solve.py has no lib.codec.v3_plan / inner_scripts call (D20-D21 needed none because every carrier was plain). Do it in the next solver-authoring pass.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"php-cli\", \"concept\": \"PHP CLI for lint/tokenize\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y php-cli  (php -l, token_get_all; never run fixtures). PHP is a carried language since D8.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"lua-unluac\", \"concept\": \"Lua interpreter + bytecode decompiler\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y lua5.4 luajit ; unluac.jar from https://sourceforge.net/projects/unluac/ into tools/unluac (java 25 installed) with bin/unluac wrapper. Needed if a luac-compiled carrier variant of the D9 Lua fixtures appears.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xsltproc-cabextract-yq\", \"concept\": \"XML/CAB/YAML helpers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y xsltproc cabextract ; yq: pip install yq into .venv (jq wrapper; jq installed). xsltproc only for --noout lint, never to apply a stylesheet.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"leaf-ext-list\", \"concept\": \"nested-zip sniff skips unknown leaf extensions\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"_LEAF_EXT in solve.py still lacks .lua .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb .ahk .gs .csx .groovy .yml (and future .tcl .r .kts .java .jsp .ipynb .go .rs .awk .tf .xsl .reg .inf). Speed only (~1 s); prefer sniffing PK magic over an extension list.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"new-synthetic-label-family\", \"concept\": \"code-shape labels for a new language (D2-D7 style)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Polyglot days have been plan-verbatim since D8, but an 'advanced <lang>' set (like bash-advanced) would bring feature/primitive or control/style labels, and OLD label families can flip regime (batch expansion D15/D16). Apply playbook NAMING LAWS; probe one field per submit; check started_at/run_for_time first.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"family-name-underscore\", \"concept\": \"host-type families like polyglot-github_actions / host-<profile>-<lang>\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Keep the longest-known-suffix field parse; derive the family prefix from the contract ids, never from the file stem (D14 msbuild_xml). D17 added `polyglot-auto_hotkey` (campaign AUTO_HOTKEY-, url host auto_hotkey-..). D18: `polyglot-google_apps_script` (campaign GOOGLE_APPS_SCRIPT-, url host google_apps_script-..) while its host file is hyphenated `host-google-docs-sidebar-google-apps-script` (profile google_docs_sidebar). D19: `polyglot-csharp_script` (campaign CSHARP_SCRIPT-, url host csharp_script-..) and host `host-aspx-inline-csharp-csharp-script` (profile aspx_inline_csharp, file extension .csx although the bytes are an ASPX page). D20: `polyglot-groovy` (campaign GROOVY-), hosts `host-jenkins-pipeline-groovy` (profile jenkins_pipeline) and `host-classic-asp-vbscript` (profile classic_asp, language vbscript, campaign VBSCRIPT-, file .vbs although the bytes are an ASP page). D21: `polyglot-github_actions` (campaign GITHUB_ACTIONS-, url host github_actions-.., file_path /tmp/huntress-github_actions/..), no host file.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"tcl-r-interpreters\", \"concept\": \"tclsh / Rscript for syntax checks\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y tcl (small); r-base-core is ~100 MB, install only on an R day. Static reading is enough for v=3 plans.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"applescript-scpt\", \"concept\": \"compiled AppleScript (.scpt FasdUAS) disassembly\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Jinmo/applescript-disassembler into tools/ (pure python). D13 shipped source .applescript only; a compiled variant would hide the marker in UTF-16/MacRoman strings.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"js-deob-extras\", \"concept\": \"synchrony / JSFuck decoding\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"npm i deobfuscator (synchrony CLI) into tools/npm; webcrack (installed) already handles obfuscator.io; JSFuck/JJencode via js_sandbox capture of the final call.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ps-deob-modules\", \"concept\": \"PowerDecode / PSDecode for pwsh\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Malandrone/PowerDecode and https://github.com/R3MRUM/PSDecode into tools/ (pwsh 7.6.6 installed). refinery ps1 covers most; these add layer-by-layer IEX override tracing.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xlm-standalone\", \"concept\": \"XLMMacroDeobfuscator CLI\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python XLMMacroDeobfuscator  (refinery xlmdeobf is an inlined port and already works; standalone gives --sort-formulas/--extract-only).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dotnet-script\", \"concept\": \"csx inspection\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D19 shipped .csx source only (static read was enough). Install dotnet-script only if a csx variant needs `#load`/`#r` resolution: dotnet tool install --tool-path tools/dotnet-tools dotnet-script (parse only; ilspycmd covers compiled InstallUtil/MSBuild/Assembly.Load payloads).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"git-repo-hooks-route\", \"concept\": \"repository-level auto-run surfaces: git hooks, filter/diff drivers, husky, pre-commit, devcontainer, submodules\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Supply-chain persistence next to CI: repo_hooks(members)->[{surface, trigger, command, lang}]: `.git/hooks/{pre-commit,post-checkout,post-merge,pre-push}` (shebang -> lang), `.git/config` `[core] hooksPath`, `[filter \\\"x\\\"] clean/smudge = ..` + `.gitattributes` `* filter=x`, `[diff \\\"x\\\"] textconv`, `[core] fsmonitor = ..`, `.husky/*`, `.pre-commit-config.yaml` `repos[].hooks[].entry` + `language:`, `.gitmodules` url/update=!cmd, `.devcontainer/devcontainer.json` postCreate/postStart (reuse json_scripts), `.vscode/tasks.json` `runOn: folderOpen`. ATT&CK hints T1195.002, T1546 (event-triggered), T1059.x. Gate: synthetic repo fixtures; D1-D21 unchanged.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"launchd-plist-route\", \"concept\": \"macOS launchd / plist persistence (XML and binary plist)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"OS-side 'keeps coming back' sibling of D13 AppleScript. plist_scripts(name, data)->[{label, program_arguments, run_at_load, keep_alive, start_interval, lang}] for XML plists (`<key>ProgramArguments</key><array><string>/bin/sh</string><string>-c</string><string>..</string>`) and binary `bplist00` (pure-Python parser: offset table, object refs; ints, strings ASCII/UTF-16BE, arrays, dicts, data, bools), `LaunchAgents`/`LaunchDaemons` path hints, `osascript -e` bodies -> AppleScript route. ATT&CK T1543.001/.004, T1647. Gate: plistlib-generated XML+binary fixtures round-trip (plistlib is stdlib; check ALLOWED_IMPORTS, else hand-parse).\"}\n]\n```\n","numLines":76,"startLine":176,"totalLines":251}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018xoUhfoYnEmAP4Pix7V4LS","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
