 attempts):\npython-exec-onion-static, evidence-type-router, file-registry-telemetry-reconcile, build-manifest-hooks. Pending after 1\nunfinished attempt (cost 0): cloud-iac-userdata-route, yaml-scalar-carrier-twists.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"Priority-1 order for D22: the D21 theme the bytes did not carry yet\n(GHA trigger/trust model, schedule persistence), the next CI YAML sibling, GitHub action/reusable-workflow handoffs; then\ninjection/secrets, k8s/IaC carriers, YAML carrier twists, repo hooks, launchd.\"\"\",\"\"\"Priority-1 order for D23: the D22 theme the bytes did not carry yet\n(installer setup-vs-payload actions + handoffs), an NSIS carrier twist (`!define`/StrCpy appends/`$\\\\` escapes), the next\ninstaller language (Inno Setup), WiX/MSI custom actions; then compiled installers, OS package scripts, package-manager\nmanifests, IaC, YAML twists, Electron/Squirrel.\"\"\")\n# json\nm=re.search(r\"```json\\n(.*?)\\n```\",s,re.S)\ngaps=json.loads(m.group(1))\nbuilt={\"gha-trigger-trust-model\",\"ci-schedule-persistence-model\",\"ci-yaml-sibling-route\",\"github-action-definition-route\",\"ci-expression-injection-secrets\",\"k8s-helm-manifest-route\",\"git-repo-hooks-route\",\"launchd-plist-route\",\"build-manifest-hooks\"}\ngaps=[g for g in gaps if g[\"id\"] not in built]\nby={g[\"id\"]:g for g in gaps}\nby[\"cloud-iac-userdata-route\"][\"priority\"]=2\nby[\"yaml-scalar-carrier-twists\"][\"priority\"]=3\nby[\"yaml-scalar-carrier-twists\"][\"detail\"]+=\" (D22 moved on to NSIS; keep for a YAML-language twist in timed variants.)\"\nby[\"solver-lib-v3-fallback\"][\"detail\"]=by[\"solver-lib-v3-fallback\"][\"detail\"].replace(\"STILL OPEN after D21: the D21 solve.py\",\"STILL OPEN after D22: the D22 solve.py (byte-identical D21 copy)\").replace(\"(D20-D21 needed none\",\"(D20-D22 needed none\")\nby[\"family-name-underscore\"][\"detail\"]+=\" D22: `polyglot-nsis` (campaign NSIS-, url host nsis-.., file_path /tmp/huntress-nsis/..), no host file.\"\nby[\"leaf-ext-list\"][\"detail\"]=by[\"leaf-ext-list\"][\"detail\"].replace(\".groovy .yml (\",\".groovy .yml .nsi (\").replace(\".reg .inf)\",\".reg .inf .iss .wxs)\")\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"installer-action-model\",\"concept\":\"installer scripts: separate real setup actions from payload behaviour and list every cross-language handoff (NSIS / Inno / WiX)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D22 prompt 'Separate the real setup actions from the modeled payload behavior, and recover every cross-language handoff' + base id `installer-script-chain` -- D22 bytes carried only Name/OutFile/Section/StrCpy, so a variant/next day adding real installer statements would ask new suffixes (`-setup-actions`, `-payload-actions`, `-handoff`, `-handoff-count`, `-next-stage`). installer_actions(name, src)->[{section/function, op, args, kind ('setup'|'payload'|'ui'), lang_to, target}] for NSIS (`SetOutPath`, `File [/oname=]`, `WriteUninstaller`, `CreateDirectory`, `CreateShortCut` (setup; $SMSTARTUP/$SMPROGRAMS\\\\\\\\Startup = persistence T1547.001), `WriteRegStr/WriteRegDWORD HKLM|HKCU Software\\\\\\\\Microsoft\\\\\\\\Windows\\\\\\\\CurrentVersion\\\\\\\\Uninstall\\\\\\\\..` (setup) vs `..\\\\\\\\Run`/`RunOnce` (payload persistence), `Exec`/`ExecWait`/`ExecShell [open|runas]`, `nsExec::Exec[ToLog|ToStack]`, `ExecDos::exec`, `inetc::get`/`NSISdl::download`/`INetC::post` (T1105), `System::Call 'kernel32::..'`, `!system` (compile-time!), `.onInit`/`.onInstSuccess`/`un.onUninstSuccess` callbacks; Inno `[Run]`/`[UninstallRun]`/`[Registry]`/`[Code] Exec/ShellExec/DownloadTemporaryFile`; WiX `CustomAction` ExeCommand/Script/DllEntry. Handoff = command line whose image is an interpreter (powershell[.exe] -enc/-File, pwsh, cscript/wscript //E:jscript, mshta, cmd /c, rundll32 javascript:, msiexec /i, regsvr32 /i:, python, node, bash) -> next_language spelled like v=3 plans (powershell, jscript, vbscript, batch, python, nodejs, bash). Reuse lib.codec declared_spawns/spawn_parent_candidates and handoff-chain-resolve; installer_answer(actions, field, accepted_values, what=). Gate: synthetic NSIS/Inno/WiX fixtures with known setup vs payload splits + every D1-D22 member (D22 nsi -> only the StrCpy, no handoff).\"},\n {\"id\":\"nsis-string-define-fold\",\"concept\":\"NSIS carrier twists: !define/${X} substitution, StrCpy appends, $\\\\ escapes, alternate quotes and comment forms\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D22 NSIS carriers were plain (`StrCpy $0 \\\"<data>\\\"`); the D18/D19-style twist on the newest language would hide the descriptor in NSIS string semantics. nsis_strings(src)->{var/define: value}: `!define NAME \\\"..\\\"` / `!define /date` / `!define /math` (ignore), `${NAME}` substitution (recursive, defines may be redefined with `!undef`), `StrCpy $0 \\\"part1\\\"` then `StrCpy $0 \\\"$0part2\\\"` / `StrCpy $0 \\\"$0${X}\\\"` appends (and `StrCpy $1 $0 len start` slicing), `Push`/`Pop` stack handoffs, `$R0-$R9`/`$0-$9`/`Var /GLOBAL x` + `$x`, quotes `\\\"..\\\"` `'..'` `` `..` `` (any may wrap the other two), escapes `$\\\\\\\"` `$\\\\'` `$\\\\`` `$\\\\r` `$\\\\n` `$\\\\t` and `$$` = literal `$`, line continuation `\\\\` at EOL, comments `;` `#` and `/* .. */` (the HUNTRESS marker may sit in any of them or be split across lines), `!macro`/`!insertmacro` bodies with `${param}`, `!include` of a sibling member, `LangString`. Then peel the joined value with lib.codec v3 peel. Gate: each twist applied to the D22 members peels back to the same plan; D1-D22 unchanged.\"},\n {\"id\":\"inno-setup-iss-route\",\"concept\":\"Inno Setup `.iss` scripts (sections + Pascal Script [Code]) as the next installer language\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Installer sibling of D22 NSIS (cf. D12 AutoIt -> D17 AutoHotkey, D20 Jenkins -> D21 GHA). Verify lib.codec.v3_plan/find_codecs on a fixture battery wrapping D22-style plans in .iss: marker in `;` (section comments) and `//`, `{ }`, `(* *)` (Pascal [Code]); descriptor forms `const descriptor_<8hex> = '..';`, `var Descriptor: String; .. Descriptor := '..' + '..';` (Pascal `''` escape inside single quotes, `#13#10`/`#$41` char literals concatenated with `+`), `#define Descriptor \\\"..\\\"` ISPP + `{#Descriptor}` expansion, `[Setup] AppName=`/`[Messages]` values, `[Run] Filename: \\\"{cmd}\\\"; Parameters: \\\"/c ..\\\"` and `[Code] Exec(ExpandConstant('{sys}\\\\\\\\..'), '..', '', SW_HIDE, ewWaitUntilTerminated, ResultCode)`. inno_strings(src) folds the concatenations. Family guess `polyglot-inno_setup` (campaign INNO_SETUP-..). Gate: battery peels to plans; D1-D22 unchanged.\"},\n {\"id\":\"wix-msi-custom-action-route\",\"concept\":\"WiX `.wxs` source and built `.msi` databases: custom-action scripts as cross-language handoffs\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"MSI is the native Windows installer; its custom actions are inline VBScript/JScript (types 37/38/53/54 = script in property/Binary, 5/6 = JScript/VBS from Binary, 34/50 = EXE command lines). wix_actions(src)->[{id, type, script_lang, body, exe_command, sequence, condition}] over `<CustomAction Id Script=\\\"vbscript|jscript\\\">` CDATA bodies, `BinaryKey`+`<Binary SourceFile>` (resolve to a sibling member), `ExeCommand`, `<Property Id Value>` substitutions `[PROP]`/`[#file]`/`[INSTALLDIR]`, `<InstallExecuteSequence><Custom Action After|Before Condition>`. For `.msi`: olefile streams; decode MSI stream names (chars 0x3800-0x47FF pack two base-64 symbols `0-9A-Za-z._`, 0x4800-0x483F one, leading 0x4840 = table), read `_StringPool`/`_StringData` + `_Tables`/`_Columns` and the CustomAction/Binary/Property tables (rows column-major, string refs 2 or 3 bytes), Binary stream bytes -> script text. Then marker/Codec scan per body (VBS/JS routes). Gate: synthetic wxs + a hand-built tiny msi (olefile write is not available -> build the OLE bytes in the test or ship a generated fixture); D1-D22 unchanged.\"},\n {\"id\":\"nsis-compiled-installer-extract\",\"concept\":\"compiled NSIS (and Inno) setup EXEs: recover the embedded script strings and files without running them\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"A timed variant or the next day may ship the BUILT `huntress-<8hex>.exe` named by D22's OutFile. NSIS: PE overlay holds firstheader (flags u32, `EF BE AD DE`, `NullsoftInst`, header_size, archive_size), then the header block (u32 length with high bit = compressed; zlib raw deflate / bzip2 / LZMA `5D 00 00` props, or one solid stream) holding the section/entry tables and a string table (UTF-16LE when the installer is Unicode, NSIS 3 `Unicode True` as in D22; codes 1-4 = NS_LANG/SHELL/VAR/SKIP escapes). nsis_extract(data)->{strings:[..], files:[(name, bytes)], unicode(bool)}: find firstheader at 512-byte-aligned offsets, decompress the header, split the string table, scan strings for HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS markers / descriptors; files from the data block. Prefer `7z l`/`7z x` (7-Zip 26.00 INSTALLED) as an oracle only (check whether it still lists `[NSIS].nsi`); keep the lib path pure stdlib (zlib, bz2, lzma). Inno: detect `Inno Setup Setup Data (x.y.z)` and report 'unsupported, use innoextract' (innoextract MISSING). Gate: a fixture assembled in the test (firstheader + zlib header with a UTF-16LE marker string); D1-D22 unchanged.\"},\n {\"id\":\"linux-package-maintainer-scripts\",\"concept\":\"deb / rpm / PKGBUILD / APKBUILD maintainer scripts as installer-chain carriers\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Linux side of 'installer script chain'. pkg_scripts(name, data)->[{format, hook (preinst|postinst|prerm|postrm|config|triggers|%pre|%post|%preun|%postun|%pretrans|%posttrans|%trigger*|pre_install|post_install|post_upgrade), interpreter, body}]: `.deb` = ar (`!<arch>\\\\n`, 60-byte headers) -> `control.tar.gz|xz|zst` (tarfile handles gz/xz; zst -> report) -> scripts; `.rpm` = 96-byte lead `ED AB EE DB`, signature header (8-byte aligned) then main header (`8E AD E8 01`, index entries tag/type/offset/count) -> tags PREIN 1023, POSTIN 1024, PREUN 1025, POSTUN 1026, PREINPROG 1085.., TRIGGERSCRIPTS 1065, PRETRANS 1151, POSTTRANS 1152; `.spec` text `%post -p /bin/sh` sections; Arch `PKGBUILD` `install=x.install` + `post_install() {..}`; Alpine `.pre-install`/`.post-install`. Bodies -> bash/python route + marker scan. ATT&CK T1546.016 (installer packages), T1059.004. Gate: in-test built ar/tar + minimal rpm header fixtures; D1-D22 unchanged.\"},\n {\"id\":\"macos-pkg-installer-scripts\",\"concept\":\"macOS flat `.pkg` (xar) Distribution JavaScript and preinstall/postinstall scripts\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Installer sibling on macOS (cf. D13 AppleScript). macpkg_scripts(data)->[{path, kind (distribution_js|preinstall|postinstall|payload), lang, body}]: xar header (`xar!`, u16 header size, u16 version, u64 toc_len_compressed, u64 toc_len_uncompressed, u32 checksum alg), zlib TOC XML -> <file> entries with <data><offset><length><encoding style=application/x-gzip|x-bzip2>, heap after TOC; `Distribution` XML `<installer-gui-script>` `<script>` CDATA JS (`system.run('/bin/sh', ..)`, `installation-check`/`volume-check` functions) -> JS route; `Scripts` member = gzip cpio (odc `070707` / newc `070701`) -> preinstall/postinstall shebang -> bash/python/osascript route. ATT&CK T1546.016, T1059.002/.004/.007. Gate: in-test built xar + cpio fixtures (pure stdlib zlib/gzip); D1-D22 unchanged.\"},\n {\"id\":\"package-manager-install-manifests\",\"concept\":\"Chocolatey / NuGet / Scoop / winget / Homebrew / MSIX-ClickOnce install manifests and their install scripts\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Package-manager installers run scripts too. pkgmgr_scripts(members)->[{manager, hook, lang, body_or_url}]: `.nupkg` (zip) `tools/chocolateyInstall.ps1|chocolateyBeforeModify.ps1|chocolateyUninstall.ps1`, NuGet `tools/install.ps1|init.ps1`, `.nuspec` XML; Scoop JSON `pre_install`/`post_install`/`installer.script`/`uninstaller.script` (string OR array of lines -> join with \\\\n -> PowerShell route), `url`/`hash`; winget YAML `InstallerUrl`, `InstallerType`, `InstallerSwitches.Custom`; Homebrew `class X < Formula` `def install`/`def post_install` + cask `postflight do .. system_command` (Ruby route); MSIX `.appinstaller` `<MainPackage Uri=>`, ClickOnce `.application` `<deploymentProvider codebase=>`. Reuse json_scripts / lib.codec yaml route. ATT&CK T1195.002, T1059.001, T1105. Gate: fixtures wrapping D22-style plans; D1-D22 unchanged.\"},\n {\"id\":\"electron-asar-squirrel-route\",\"concept\":\"Electron `app.asar` archives and Squirrel/NuGet updater packages as JS carriers\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Installer-delivered Electron apps hide Node JS in `resources/app.asar`: Chromium pickle header (u32 4, u32 header_size, u32 pickle size, u32 json_len, JSON `{files:{name:{offset,size,unpacked?}}}`, file data after header padded to 4) -> list + extract `package.json` `main`, `*.js`; Squirrel `RELEASES` + `.nupkg` (zip) with `lib/net45/*.exe` and `Update.exe --processStart` command lines. asar_files(data)->{path: bytes}; then Node/JS route + marker scan. Gate: in-test built asar fixture; D1-D22 unchanged.\"}\n]\nids={g[\"id\"] for g in gaps}\nfor n in new:\n    assert n[\"id\"] not in ids\norder=[n for n in new if n[\"priority\"]==1]+[g for g in gaps if g[\"priority\"]==1]+[n for n in new if n[\"priority\"]==2]+[g for g in gaps if g[\"priority\"]==2]+[n for n in new if n[\"priority\"]==3]+[g for g in gaps if g[\"priority\"]==3]\nout=\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in order)+\"\\n]\"\njson.loads(out)\ns=s[:m.start(1)]+out+s[m.end(1):]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(len(order),[ (g['id'],g['priority'],g['action']) for g in order])\nEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3991,"cache_read_input_tokens":129548,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_