astery is now **6 sets** (8502 ids)). The prompt (\"separate the real setup actions from the modeled payload behavior, recover\nevery cross-language handoff\") had nothing behind it: no File/ExecWait/nsExec/registry lines, only the plan's next_language.\nD21-night gaps: 8 built, build-manifest-hooks given up (2 attempts), cloud-iac-userdata-route + yaml-scalar-carrier-twists\nstill pending; the queue below is rebuilt from the D22 direction (installers/packaging: NSIS twists, Inno, WiX/MSI, compiled\ninstallers, OS package scripts, package-manager manifests).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  asked). Two threads now run: (a) **build/CI supply-chain hosts**\"\"\",\"\"\"  asked), D22 NSIS installer script (base `installer-script-chain`; \"setup actions vs payload, every cross-language\n  handoff\" -- never asked). Three threads now run: (c) **installers/packaging** (NSIS seen D22 -> Inno Setup `.iss` Pascal\n  `[Code]`, WiX `.wxs`/MSI CustomAction scripts, compiled NSIS/Inno exes, `.inf`, deb/rpm maintainer scripts, macOS `.pkg`\n  Distribution JS, Chocolatey/Scoop/winget manifests, MSIX/ClickOnce/Squirrel); (a) **build/CI supply-chain hosts**\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- ~10 drops left (D22-D31).\"\"\",\"\"\"- ~9 drops left (D23-D31).\"\"\")\n# table rows\nrep(\"\"\"| 81 | GitHub action definitions\"\"\",\"\"\"| 82 | NSIS installer script `.nsi` | seen D22 | line-1 `; HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..`, `Unicode True`, `Name \"Huntress Analysis <8hex>\"`, `OutFile \"huntress-<8hex>.exe\"`, `Section` / `StrCpy $0 \"<data>\"` / `SectionEnd` (no descriptor NAME); family `polyglot-nsis`. Real-world cues: `!define`/`${X}`, `!include MUI2.nsh`, `!insertmacro MUI_PAGE_*`, `Function .onInit`, `SetOutPath $INSTDIR`, `File /oname=`, `ExecWait`/`Exec`/`ExecShell`, `nsExec::ExecToLog`, `inetc::get`/`NSISdl::download`, `WriteRegStr HKLM ..\\\\Run`, `CreateShortCut $SMSTARTUP`, `$\\\\\"` escapes | carried V3_MARK (unchanged); plan `language=nsis`, campaign `NSIS-<8hex>`, url host `nsis-<10hex>`, attack T1059